# Pass "incompat-original": the original mod this one declares itself incompatible with, alone beside it.
#
# ancientbld.core, Workshop 2566355159 - "Ancient" Buildings by SyndicateGamingNetwork, which declares 1.3
# and nothing further. About.xml names it in incompatibleWith because the two define the same five defNames.
# RimWorld does not refuse two mods that do: it keeps one copy of each and, as the first run showed, logs nothing about it. This pass stages
# both and plays 05-original-mod-incompatibility, which asserts that the original still loads with its 1.4-removed field, so a green run says the
# incompatibility is still worth declaring.
#
# The item has to be in the WSL install's Workshop cache before this pass can stage it. That is a download,
# so it goes through Use-Wsl.ps1 like any other work on the machine (PickleTools/Headless/README.md, "The
# lock is about the machine"). It has not been downloaded.
ancientbld.core   2566355159
